@@ -4,4 +4,26 @@ Consumes `price.changed` events and pushes prices to the marketplace partner's p
 Only brands that are eligible for the website are sent; the eligible list comes from the
 nightly warehouse export `eligible_brands.csv` (see `warehouse-sql/procs/eligible_brands.sql`).
 
+## Admin endpoints
+
+Served on `ADMIN_PORT` (8081) behind the `price-sync-admin` Service.
+
+- `GET /healthz`
+- `POST /reload-eligible-brands` — re-reads `eligible_brands.csv` without a restart.
+
+Two things to know before relying on the reload:
+
+- **It reloads one replica per call.** Prod runs 4 replicas (`deploy-config/overlays/prod/
+  price-sync.yaml`) behind one load-balanced admin Service, so a single POST reaches a
+  single pod and the others keep the old list. The reply includes `instance` so you can see
+  which pod answered; call it until you have seen every pod, or address pods directly.
+- **It reloads the file, not the warehouse.** `eligible_brands.csv` is only regenerated by
+  the 02:00 UTC `warehouse-brand-exports` job (`deploy-config/jobs/schedules.yaml`). A
+  `web_eligible` change made in the warehouse today is not in the CSV until that job runs,
+  so reloading first will just re-read the same list. Check `source_modified` in the reply:
+  if it is not newer than your change, the export has not caught up yet.
+
+A failed reload (missing or unparseable export) returns 500 and leaves the current list in
+place, so a half-written export cannot empty the eligible list.
+
 Run tests: `python -m unittest discover -s tests`
